Items that do not qualify for the CAN$20 exemption include the following:
 tobacco;
 books;
 periodicals;
 magazines;
 alcoholic beverages; and
 goods ordered through a Canadian post office box or a Canadian intermediary.

Items that do not qualify for the CAN$60 gift exemption include the following:
 tobacco;
 alcoholic beverages;
 advertising material; and
 items sent by a business.
 As well, the CAN$60 gift exemption cannot be combined with the CAN$20 exemption that is available on most items valued at CAN$20 or less.

There are exceptions from the prohibition on restricted goods and industrial goods relating to:
 Temporary media exports;
 International nuclear safeguards verification;
 The Government of Canada;
 The Chemical Weapons Convention;
 The International Space Station;
 Software updates;
 Civil aircraft;
 Aircraft and ship stores;
 Maintenance, repair or operation of aircraft of Canadian and US air carriers;
 Consumer communication devices;
 Personal effects.
